If we take every 12th note we observe another interesting pattern, that highlights the enharmonic equivalents: Fbb, Eb, D# and so on. The distance between the notes is Diminished Second (enharmonic equivalents of Unison), which sharpens the previous note in chromatic scale. You can tap on any note in the table above to highlight its enharmonics.

